- Before releasing the new complete TI-85 key legends:
  - Check 2nd/ALPHA combinations against actual calculator input, including
    lowercase, equals, and space; rendering has been visually reviewed only.
  - Review the native GUI's labels and click targets during calculator use.
  - Review the web keypad on a small mobile display.
  - Full printed legends are now transcribed from the maintainer's photograph
    and shared between the original vector skin and web keypad. Native key
    positions/click rectangles and emulator key codes are retained.

- Exercise the native GUI and calculator link transfers on NetBSD. Its CI build
  now passes after installing the matching native X11 runtime/development sets.

- Linking between 2 tilem instances
- Sound
- Rewrite macro (parser and tokens).
- Add scripting (lua or something else?)
